          },
          "name": "MCP tools - send_message, send_file, send_audio_message, download_media",
          "visibility": "public"
        },
        {
          "_type": "UMLComponent",
          "_id": "VzhZtEsOhTEONTCvxGkY",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "6T7C+jb/gxPvviWpkQF6"
          },
          "name": "scope note - opencode only, NOT wired into the campaign pipeline or k3s",
          "visibility": "public"
        },
        {
          "_type": "UMLNote",
          "_id": "2nE6aqhPb6gElRlOE5i6",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "6T7C+jb/gxPvviWpkQF6"
          },
          "text": "opencode only: nothing in the campaign pipeline or the k3s cluster\ncalls these tools.\nInstall: brew install go, clone lharries/whatsapp-mcp under\n~/ZCodeProject/tools, then go build the bridge.\nThe bridge keeps WhatsApp Web multi-device state in a local SQLite\nstore and prints a QR code to pair.\nPairing needs the user's phone (WhatsApp > Linked devices); the\nre-link window is about 20 days.\nSends are user driven; the agent never sends on its own."
        },
        {
          "_type": "UMLDependency",
          "_id": "DFDnclvjSBKf8ozFdRgH",
